    "reply": "The retrieved dataset details specific sequence variants mapped to the BRCA1 transcript NM_007294.4 across multiple coding regions [1][30]. These entries document individual missense substitutions characterized by distinct ClinVar accession identifiers [2][29].\n\n## ClinVar Sequence Variants\n\nSequenceVariant ClinVar:1001081 is identified by the nomenclature NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.353T>C (p.Leu118Pro) [3]. The record SequenceVariant ClinVar:1009204 corresponds to NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.500C>T (p.Thr167Ile) [21]. Another variant entry is SequenceVariant ClinVar:1010063, designated as NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.641A>T (p.Asp214Val) [26].\n\n## Intermediate Coding Alterations\n\nThe cataloged variation SequenceVariant ClinVar:1009121 represents NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.778A>G (p.Lys260Glu) [20]. Additional documentation provides SequenceVariant ClinVar:1007698 with the notation NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.1199A>T (p.Asp400Val) [17]. A proximate missense change is SequenceVariant ClinVar:1002154, defined as NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.1226T>G (p.Val409Gly) [4].\n\n## Downstream Exonic Changes\n\nFurther downstream, SequenceVariant ClinVar:1010509 denotes NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.1328A>G (p.Lys443Arg) [27]. In the same region, SequenceVariant ClinVar:1010603 is termed NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.1331G>T (p.Ser444Ile) [28]. The accession SequenceVariant record ClinVar:1010631 lacks an explicit transcript-level designation in the findings [29]. Near the carboxy-terminal portion, SequenceVariant ClinVar:1010734 is listed as NM_007294.4(BRCA1):c.4840C>G (p.Pro1614Ala) [30].",
